      "head": "codex/ps235-validator-followup",
      "title": "Skip empty Markdown array scans and add context coverage",
      "body": "Skip element scans for empty code and link arrays in Markdown parse contexts while preserving the existing array-type and malformed-element checks. Apply the change accepted in [PSStyleGuide #235](https://github.com/franklesniak/PSStyleGuide/pull/235) to TerraformStyleGuide's prose, table-cell and list-item validation.\n\nThe permanent SelfTest adds 109 cases that call the real parser and structural decoder. They cover valid empty and populated arrays, missing/null fields, wrong types and malformed elements. Rejected inputs must produce no partial context, and the test restores its temporary parser wrapper. Within these three files, the only repository-specific differences remain the existing T1 provenance fixture and dependency-guide scope sentence; touched metadata is current.\n\nValidation of the candidate bytes, unchanged by the normal commit:\n\n- Windows PowerShell 7.6.5 and Linux PowerShell 7.6.3: 109 cases each, with 19 accepts and 90 refusals; fresh parser/decoder calls and restoration verified.\n- Both changed PowerShell files: zero parser errors and zero PSScriptAnalyzer 1.24.0 warnings/errors on both platforms.\n- Staged preflight, ordinary Markdown checks, all eleven pre-commit checks including the full mutation SelfTest, and normal commit hooks passed.\n- Independent review of the exact source and focused results found no material issue.\n- All five committed-input checks passed: accepted maintenance classification, accepted content, current-date finalization, metadata classification and proposed-policy diagnostics.\n- The ordinary dependency audit was CLEAN for both installed roots, with no findings or exception grants. Separate native-main reads confirmed the accepted authority before and after the audit; its offline result does not itself discover external revocations or later ref changes.\n\nNative reviews, CI and paired acceptance remain separate gates. This change makes no performance claim and does not change generator output, dependencies, workflow permissions or review setup.\n",
